Yes. The ending can be the release point.

While the prayer is being spoken, intention is still being formed and held. When it ends, the posture can shift from asking/forming to acting/receiving/observing.

\text{intention} \rightarrow \text{articulation} \rightarrow \text{release} \rightarrow \text{action} \rightarrow \text{feedback}

In that sense, the prayer ending is not the termination of the process. It is the handoff from inner state to outer world.

Same pattern as drawing a bow: the tension matters, but nothing flies until you let go.